Package: internet-monitor
Version: 1.0.0
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>=3.10), python3-venv, python3-pip, iputils-ping, adduser, systemd
Recommends: libnotify-bin
Maintainer: Internet Monitor Maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>
Homepage: https://github.com/example/internet-monitor
Description: Lightweight Internet latency and connectivity monitor
 Internet Monitor continuously measures latency, packet loss, jitter, and
 connectivity to a configurable set of targets (your gateway, public DNS
 resolvers, or any host you choose). History is stored locally in SQLite;
 there is no cloud dependency.
 .
 Runs as an unprivileged systemd service (internet-monitor) with a local
 web dashboard and REST API bound to 127.0.0.1, plus an `internet-monitor`
 CLI. Installing this package fetches the pure-Python backend dependencies
 (FastAPI, uvicorn, aiosqlite, etc.) from PyPI during configuration, so an
 internet connection is required at install time.
